Q(2,'explanation','The deliberate per-guess cost comes mainly from the password hash parameters. Salting is designed to prevent shared precomputation, not to act as a work factor.',0)
Q(2,'workedExample','Distinct random salts prevent identical passwords from having directly comparable stored hashes and prevent one hash evaluation from checking all accounts. Large salts defeat practical universal precomputed tables. A password recovered elsewhere can still be tested as a candidate for another account. Combine salts with a costly password hash; they are not secret.')
