Q(6,'workedExample','Under the stated constant-throughput model, 10^8 / 1,000 = 100,000 seconds, or about 27.8 hours. The SHA256 comparison is 10^8 / 10^10 = 0.01 seconds. Exhausting that same list for one million distinct salts scales the total checks by one million if throughput remains fixed. This is total modeled work, not a measured campaign or guaranteed time to recover a password: candidate order, reuse, parallelism and resource constraints matter.')
Q(7,'explanation','HKDF is fast and adds no deliberately costly password work factor. Use an appropriate salted password KDF before deriving subkeys.',1)
