Q(7,'explanation','Correct if the previous derivation started from strong secret material and outputs are long enough. HKDF does not create missing entropy; use purpose-specific context.',4)
Q(7,'workedExample','HKDF is appropriate for a securely established X25519 secret, a random master key, or sufficiently long secret KDF output derived from strong inputs. X25519\'s roughly 128-bit classical attack strength is not the same quantity as raw output length or entropy. A uniformly random six-digit PIN has log2(1,000,000) ≈ 19.93 bits; human choices can be weaker. HKDF cannot turn a guessable password/PIN into a high-entropy secret.')
